# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the gve concurrency harness.
#
# The nanos runtime queue is a lock-free MPMC ring built on
# compare_and_swap_32 (inline-asm in x86_64/machine.h), which TSan cannot see
# through, so it reports the queue's internal head/slot synchronisation as
# races.  The queue is a separately-vetted runtime primitive, not the driver
# code under test, so its internals are suppressed; the driver's own
# lock-protected state (head, desc_tail, tags, compl_head, ctx_head) uses the
# __atomic spinlock from shim/lock.h and is analysed normally.
race:enqueue
race:dequeue
race:queue_data
